{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/748899-you-must-obey-nightmare","id":748899,"title":"You Must Obey Nightmare","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-02T04:40:28-08:00","id":748899,"title":"You Must Obey Nightmare","content":"How is You Must Obey not overpowered compared to, say, You Are Not Alone which simply subtracts dice from a Perception roll? Especially when combined with You Cannot Wake Up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T07:05:15-08:00","id":749097,"title":"","content":"Easy. YMO relies on breaking points. Its a glorified &quot;do what I say because I'm scary&quot; intimidation tactic. If you try to order someone to, say, break into someone's home and rob them (another breaking point for many), the power will fail, since the power's victim will likely chose to just take the breaking point and run away from the Beast. Hell, ordering a bodyguard to stand aside so you can kidnap someone would likely fail. There comes a point where breaking points aren't enough to control someone. <br /> <br /> Meanwhile, YANA is basically a single target Obfuscate power. Highly Satiety makes it so you can pretty much walk in front of someone and they won't see you. That's pretty bad ass in its own right. Why need to deal with pesky things like witnesses if you can just slip past them? The two powers are completely different - YMO is a mind control effect, while YANA is a stealth power. Completely different uses.<br /> <br /> <br /> Make no mistake, YMO is pretty powerful, and one of the better Nightmares, but it has its limits and isn't a cure all. Its not Dominate where we can rewrite memories, and its not like Majesty where people willingly do anything out of love. It certainly can't replace invisibility or attack powers, and its pretty much a blunt tool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T07:23:59-08:00","id":749117,"title":"","content":"Also, because it relies on Breaking Points, some creatures are essentially immune! I enjoyed my player's reaction when she tried to use it on a Beshilu XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}